Strict counter validation reads only the first 64 bytes without checking EOF. An oversized, malformed sidecar can therefore pass validation when its prefix forms an accepted count, contradicting the whole-counter validation promise. Minimal fix: read one byte beyond the allowed size, reject oversized files, and validate the complete accepted contents.

